r angle resolution, given that the baseline with n_phi=16 already shows low artifact, but finer phi sampling may better resolve azimuthal variations. Budget allows n_phi=32 with coarser n_pos and n_mu, which isolates the effect of phi refinement at low cost.\",\n  \"decision_reason\": \"History shows baseline (1,2,16) has ray_index 0.00442 and rel_l1 0.092, while (2,4,32) reduces artifacts but doubles cost. To identify which discretization parameter dominates, we need to increment only n_phi from baseline, keeping n_pos and n_mu minimal. This isolates the azimuthal resolution effect within budget (1*2*32=64<256) and is cheaper than testing other combinations.\"\n}", "response_id": "b155496c-0c2d-4bc3-aa2c-a996371514f4", "system_fingerprint": "a26a7955944dc5c60445bff77fac9c8e", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 457, "completion_tokens": 215, "total_tokens": 672, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 256}, "prompt_cache_hit_tokens": 256, "prompt_cache_miss_tokens": 201}, "secret_recorded": false}
